// meta_sysml_trace.hymeko — SysML v2 requirements-traceability vocabulary.
//
// Companion witness for the SMC paper (reviewer item 5 of smc_02/review_1): a
// minimal NON-robotics instance of the same canonical signed-hypergraph IR, to
// back the conclusion's claim that SysML v2 / systems-engineering traceability
// is a further instance of the same machinery (not an unmeasured aspiration).
//
// Node types are requirements and blocks (components); the trace relations are
// signed n-ary hyperedges over them:
//
//   satisfies(+ block,        - requirement)   a component satisfies a requirement
//   derives  (+ derived_req,  - source_req)     a requirement is derived from another
//   allocated_to(+ requirement, - block)        a requirement is allocated to a block
//
// Modeled on data/robotics/meta_kinematics.hymeko: plain names are node-type
// decls, `@name` decls are hyperedge types.

meta_sysml_trace {}

sysml_trace {
    elements {
        meta_element {}
        requirement: + <isa> meta_element {}
        block:       + <isa> meta_element {}
    }

    @satisfies {}
    @derives {}
    @allocated_to {}
}
